quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  4,128,"If a woman fears misconduct or desertion from her husband, there is no sin upon the couple if they mutually reconcile with a fair settlement. And reconciliation is (always) better. The souls are ever inclined to selfishness, but if you act benevolently and be God-conscious, Allah is indeed All-Aware of what you do."
  4,129,"And you will never be able to maintain (emotional) justice between (your) wives, even if you are eager to do so. So do not incline entirely (towards one) and leave the other hanging (between marriage and divorce). If you set things right and be God-conscious, Allah is indeed Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  4,130,"If the two (decide to) separate, Allah will compensate both out of His Abundance, and Allah is All-Bounteous, All-Wise."
  4,131,"And to Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. Indeed, We have commanded those given the Book before you, and you, to be God-conscious. But if you disbelieve (in Him), to Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. And Allah is All-Sufficient, All-Praised."
  4,132,"And to Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth, and Allah is Sufficient as Guardian."
  4,133,"If He wills, He can remove you altogether, O people, and bring others (in your place). And Allah is All-Capable over that."
  4,134,"Whoever desires the reward of this world (should know that) with Allah is the reward of this world and the Hereafter. And Allah is All-Hearing, All-Seeing."
